00:00Z","speed":1}],"beats":[{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:00Z","text":"Pope Leo XIV delivers homily to thousands in Uruguay, Al Jazeera reports.","cites":["news:aljazeera:99103deebe6f"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:08Z","text":"He is the first pope from the United States or North America, the first pope to be a citizen of Peru, and the second pope, following the 12th-century Pope Adrian IV, to come from an English-speaking country.","cites":["wiki:rev:1384593489:10"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:16Z","text":"Pope Leo XIV (born Robert Francis Prevost, pronounced; September 14, 1955) is the head of the Catholic Church and sovereign of Vatican City.","cites":["wiki:rev:1384593489:0"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:24Z","text":"Leo XIV was born on 14 September 1955 in Mercy Hospital and Medical Center.","cites":["wd:Q6109517:P569","wd:Q6109517:P19"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:32Z","text":"Educated at St. Augustine Seminary High School, Villanova University, Catholic Theological Union and Pontifical University of Saint Thomas Aquinas.","cites":["wd:Q6109517:P69:Q134398367","wd:Q6109517:P69:Q1466001","wd:Q6109517:P69:Q5053247","wd:Q6109517:P69:Q246887","wd:Q6109517:P69:Q246887"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:47Z","text":"11 awards on record, among them Order of the Bath (2025) and Time 100 (2026).","cites":["wd:Q6109517:P166:Q506369","wd:Q6109517:P166:Q604370"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:57Z","text":"After a successful trip to Uruguay, Pope Leo heads to Argentina, NPR reports.","cites":["news:npr:2750aa3feb24"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:01:16Z","text":"Al Jazeera headlined it: “Pope Leo XIV delivers homily to thousands in Uruguay”","cites":["news:aljazeera:99103deebe6f"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:01:27Z","text":"Sources: Al Jazeera and NPR, Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews and Wikidata. Every caption links to the evidence it rests on.","cites":["wiki:rev:1384593489:10","views:en:Pope_Leo_XIV:30d","wd:Q6109517:P569"]}],"time":"story","spotlight":{"country":"UY","lon":-55.97,"lat":-32.96,"label":"Uruguay"},"cha